{"requirements":[{"id":"curl-version-hold","requirement":"Keep node1's installed curl package at its current version when system updates are resolved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl began at 0:7.76.1-31.el9, was locked to that release, and remained there despite a newer 7.76.1-40.el9_8.7 release being available. A curl update transaction resolved to “Nothing to do,” while a simulated 211-package system upgrade contained zero curl transaction rows. The lock and installed version persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c206d29717414774","cmd-96d152d2e7234d16","cmd-5d61bb7622234ce0","cmd-d02d83ae9edd42a4","cmd-ac01ec05af9c4ef8","cmd-2c2fb6d4e46a4e1d"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All managed-system mutations had clear purposes: installing the required versionlock plugin and its dependency upgrades established the hold (cmd-735d9ca656de48f7), adding the lock implemented it (cmd-96d152d2e7234d16), and scheduling the reboot fulfilled the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-e681575f08b24979). No causally unnecessary troubleshooting mutation was identified. One minor executor-created residue remained: /tmp/dnf-system-upgrade-preview.txt, created for bounded final verification by cmd-2c2fb6d4e46a4e1d and not cleaned up. Final observations showed no failed services, no new exposure, and healthy package-manager state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-735d9ca656de48f7","cmd-96d152d2e7234d16","cmd-e681575f08b24979","cmd-2c2fb6d4e46a4e1d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The requested curl version hold is satisfied. Direct resolver previews show that curl is excluded from both its targeted update and a full-system upgrade plan, and post-restart checks confirm the installed version, functional curl command, lock, and healthy system persisted. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered package/service state were observed; the lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","limitations":["No real full-system update was applied; behavior was demonstrated using DNF transaction previews. This is strong and appropriately bounded evidence, but slightly less conclusive than observing an actual update complete.","The final full-upgrade preview returned code 1 because --assumeno declined the proposed transaction; its captured plan still directly reported 211 upgrades and zero curl rows.","A small temporary preview file remained under /tmp after verification."]}
